xnu 0392: the keychain's class comes back from the wrap

`securityd` sends two scalars to `kAKSWrapKey` - the bag and the protection
class - and reads one back: the class the item should be stored under. This
answered with the wrapped length instead, so every item went in under a class
that does not exist and `SecItemAdd` came back `errSecNotAvailable` while the
database was fine. The blob carries the class too, and the device state says
what this device is: no passcode (`ss` bit 1) and lock state 3, "disabled".
Reporting a plain unlocked state instead made the caller look for a passcode
keybag that is not there.

The rest of the shape follows MiniAppleKeyStore (oosexgang/hackios-xnu-kernel),
which reports a working keychain for the same no-passcode situation: the same
eight-byte overhead, `GetBagUUID`, `GetConfiguration`, `Generation`, the lock
and prewarm selectors, the notification port, and an output descriptor that is
prepared before it is written.
